{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unholy-shogunal-oyster","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nnormalize_ci_conclusion.sh is a pure function in shell — trivially portable, currently untestable by the Python suite.\n\n## Approach\nPort to a small Python function with unit tests; YAML call site swaps to the Python invocation. Opportunistic priority (lowest tier).\n\n## Scope\n- the script + its workflow call site + unit tests\n\n## Testing\nTable-driven unit test over all conclusion inputs (success/failure/cancelled/timed_out/neutral/skipped/unknown) asserting normalized outputs match current shell behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Python function with table-driven tests reproduces current mapping exactly.\n- [ ] Workflow calls the Python entry point; shell file deleted.","id":"9d07-99da-ce34-4c19","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["shell-migration"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Shell-to-Python Tier 1: normalize_ci_conclusion.sh"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640131116002001,"uuid":"ad0cfd58-3eb9-417b-a5be-0356d730bbf6"}